# Testing

Define testing requirements and patterns for the Next.js frontend.

## Coverage Requirements

- **Minimum:** 70% line coverage for frontend
- **Critical paths:** 90%+ for scraping pipeline, LLM abstraction, signal analysis
- Measure with built-in Next.js coverage

## Test File Naming & Location

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── SignalCard.tsx
│   └── SignalCard.test.tsx      # co-located
├── app/
│   └── articles/
│       └── page.test.tsx
└── __tests__/                   # shared test utilities
    └── test-utils.tsx
```

## Test Types & Boundaries

### Unit Tests
- Pure functions: parsing, classification, formatting
- No external dependencies (mock everything)
- Fast (< 100ms per test)
- **Frontend:** Vitest + React Testing Library

### Integration Tests
- Test interactions between components (e.g., scraper → parser → cache)
- Mock external services (HTTP, LLM APIs, database)
- **Frontend:** component + API route tests

### End-to-End Tests
- Full pipeline with real (or realistic) data
- Use Playwright for browser automation
- Run in CI on every PR
- Keep minimal — only critical user flows

## Mocking Strategies

### Scraping Tests
Mock HTTP responses, not parsing logic:

```typescript
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';

const server = setupServer(
  http.get('https://example.com/article', () => {
    return HttpResponse.html('<html><body>Article content</body></html>');
  })
);

describe('parseArticle', () => {
  it('extracts article title', async () => {
    const result = await parseArticle('https://example.com/article');
    expect(result.title).toBe('Expected Title');
  });
});
```

### LLM Tests
Mock LLM responses, test prompt construction and output parsing:

```typescript
vi.mock('@/lib/ai/provider', () => ({
  createProvider: () => ({
    generate: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({
      facts: [{ text: 'Revenue up 20%' }],
    }),
  }),
}));

describe('LLM parsing', () => {
  it('parses fact extraction response', () => {
    const mockResponse = { facts: [{ text: 'Revenue up 20%' }] };
    const result = parseExtractResponse(mockResponse);
    expect(result.facts).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(result.facts[0].text).toBe('Revenue up 20%');
  });
});
```

### Database Tests
Use test database or mock Prisma client:

```typescript
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
import { mockDeep, DeepMockProxy } from 'jest-mock-extended';

vi.mock('@prisma/client', () => ({
  PrismaClient: vi.fn(),
}));

describe('Database operations', () => {
  let prisma: DeepMockProxy<PrismaClient>;

  beforeEach(() => {
    prisma = mockDeep<PrismaClient>();
  });

  it('creates signal with correct data', async () => {
    prisma.signal.create.mockResolvedValue({
      id: '123',
      sourceUrl: 'https://example.com',
      // ... other fields
    });

    const result = await createSignal({ sourceUrl: 'https://example.com' });
    expect(result.sourceUrl).toBe('https://example.com');
  });
});
```

## Test Data Management

- **Factories:** Create test data factories for reusable test data
- **Snapshots:** Use Vitest snapshots for testing LLM output structure
- **Never commit:** Real API keys, PII, or large datasets

```typescript
export const createMockSignal = (overrides?: Partial<Signal>): Signal => ({
  id: '123',
  sourceUrl: 'https://example.com/news',
  rawText: 'Company X reported 20% revenue growth...',
  scrapedAt: new Date(),
  ...overrides,
});
```

## CI Test Requirements

All PRs must pass:
1. `pnpm lint` — linting
2. `pnpm typecheck` — type checking
3. `pnpm test` — all tests (unit + integration)
4. Coverage threshold met

## Running Tests Locally

```powershell
pnpm test                                            # all tests
pnpm test -- --watch                                 # watch mode
pnpm test -- --coverage                              # with coverage
pnpm lint                                            # linting
pnpm typecheck                                       # type checking
```
